# `prc::ImpliedVolMethod`

The root-finding algorithm `Field::implied_vol` uses.

All methods solve `BS(σ) = price` for `σ` inside the bracket `[lower_vol, upper_vol]`; the price is increasing in `σ`, so the root is unique when it exists. `Auto` and `Brent` are the same method: Brent's, which combines bisection's guaranteed bracket with the speed of inverse quadratic interpolation. `Newton` uses vega as the derivative and converges fastest from a good start but can leave the bracket where vega is tiny (deep out of the money); `Secant` avoids the derivative; `Bisection` is slow and unconditionally safe. Whatever the chosen method, if its answer does not satisfy the price tolerance, the solver falls back to bisection, so the answer is correct for every method and the choice only affects speed.

The constants `prc::Auto`, `prc::Newton`, `prc::Bisection`, `prc::Secant`, `prc::Brent` are shorthand for the enumerators.

## Fields

### `Auto`

`enumerator`, default `0`.

The default: Brent's method.

### `Newton`

`enumerator`, default `1`.

Newton's method with vega as the derivative; fastest near the root, falls back to bisection when it fails.

### `Bisection`

`enumerator`, default `2`.

Interval halving; slowest, unconditionally safe.

### `Secant`

`enumerator`, default `3`.

Derivative-free secant iteration.

### `Brent`

`enumerator`, default `4`.

Bisection safeguarded inverse-quadratic interpolation; the same as `Auto`.

## Guidance

Set as `ImpliedVolOptions::method`.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

All methods agree on a well-posed price. The price of a 25%-volatility call is inverted five ways.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace prc = fin::pricing;
namespace mod = fin::module;
using pluss::Series;

static double bs(fin::pricing::OptionType type, double S, double K, double r, double q, double T, double vol) {
  fin::module::Field f{.instrument = fin::instrument::make(type, K, T), .market = fin::market::make(S, r, q),
                       .model = fin::model::BlackScholes{.volatility = pluss::make_series({vol})},
                       .controls = {.engine = fin::module::Engine::Analytic, .risk = fin::module::Risk::PriceOnly}};
  return f.price().price.items<double>()[0];
}
static pluss::Series bsv(fin::pricing::OptionType type, const pluss::Series &spots, double K, double r, double q, double T, double vol) {
  fin::module::Field f{.instrument = fin::instrument::make(type, K, T), .market = {.spot = spots, .rate = pluss::make_series({r}), .dividend_yield = pluss::make_series({q})},
                       .model = fin::model::BlackScholes{.volatility = pluss::make_series({vol})},
                       .controls = {.engine = fin::module::Engine::Analytic, .risk = fin::module::Risk::PriceOnly}};
  return f.price().price;
}
static pluss::Series bst(fin::pricing::OptionType type, const pluss::Series &spots, const pluss::Series &tau, double K, double r, double q, double vol) {
  fin::module::Field f{.instrument = {.type = type, .strike = pluss::make_series({K}), .maturity = tau}, .market = {.spot = spots, .rate = pluss::make_series({r}), .dividend_yield = pluss::make_series({q})},
                       .model = fin::model::BlackScholes{.volatility = pluss::make_series({vol})},
                       .controls = {.engine = fin::module::Engine::Analytic, .risk = fin::module::Risk::PriceOnly}};
  return f.price().price;
}
static fin::hedging::DeltaHedgeResult hedge(const pluss::Series &path, fin::pricing::OptionType type, double K, double r, double q, double T, double vol) {
  fin::module::Field f{.instrument = fin::instrument::make(type, K, T), .market = fin::market::make(100.0, r, q),
                       .model = fin::model::BlackScholes{.volatility = pluss::make_series({vol})},
                       .controls = {.engine = fin::module::Engine::Analytic}};
  return fin::hedging::delta_hedge(f, path);
}
static double iv(double price, double S, double K, double r, double q, double T, const fin::pricing::ImpliedVolOptions &o = {}) {
  fin::module::Field f{.instrument = fin::instrument::make(fin::pricing::Call, K, T), .market = fin::market::make(S, r, q),
                       .model = fin::model::BlackScholes{.volatility = pluss::make_series({0.2})},
                       .controls = {.engine = fin::module::Engine::Analytic, .risk = fin::module::Risk::PriceOnly}};
  return f.implied_vol(pluss::make_series({price}), o).items<double>()[0];
}

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(10));
  const double S = 100.0, K = 100.0, r = 0.05, q = 0.02, T = 1.0, v = 0.2;

  const double price = bs(prc::Call, S, K, r, q, T, 0.25);
  for (const prc::ImpliedVolMethod method : {prc::Auto, prc::Newton, prc::Bisection, prc::Secant, prc::Brent}) {
    prc::ImpliedVolOptions options;
    options.method = method;
    out.writeln(static_cast<int>(method), ": implied vol =", iv(price, S, K, r, q, T, options));
  }
}
```

### Example 2

Auto is Brent: the two give the identical result.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace prc = fin::pricing;
namespace mod = fin::module;
using pluss::Series;

static double bs(fin::pricing::OptionType type, double S, double K, double r, double q, double T, double vol) {
  fin::module::Field f{.instrument = fin::instrument::make(type, K, T), .market = fin::market::make(S, r, q),
                       .model = fin::model::BlackScholes{.volatility = pluss::make_series({vol})},
                       .controls = {.engine = fin::module::Engine::Analytic, .risk = fin::module::Risk::PriceOnly}};
  return f.price().price.items<double>()[0];
}
static pluss::Series bsv(fin::pricing::OptionType type, const pluss::Series &spots, double K, double r, double q, double T, double vol) {
  fin::module::Field f{.instrument = fin::instrument::make(type, K, T), .market = {.spot = spots, .rate = pluss::make_series({r}), .dividend_yield = pluss::make_series({q})},
                       .model = fin::model::BlackScholes{.volatility = pluss::make_series({vol})},
                       .controls = {.engine = fin::module::Engine::Analytic, .risk = fin::module::Risk::PriceOnly}};
  return f.price().price;
}
static pluss::Series bst(fin::pricing::OptionType type, const pluss::Series &spots, const pluss::Series &tau, double K, double r, double q, double vol) {
  fin::module::Field f{.instrument = {.type = type, .strike = pluss::make_series({K}), .maturity = tau}, .market = {.spot = spots, .rate = pluss::make_series({r}), .dividend_yield = pluss::make_series({q})},
                       .model = fin::model::BlackScholes{.volatility = pluss::make_series({vol})},
                       .controls = {.engine = fin::module::Engine::Analytic, .risk = fin::module::Risk::PriceOnly}};
  return f.price().price;
}
static fin::hedging::DeltaHedgeResult hedge(const pluss::Series &path, fin::pricing::OptionType type, double K, double r, double q, double T, double vol) {
  fin::module::Field f{.instrument = fin::instrument::make(type, K, T), .market = fin::market::make(100.0, r, q),
                       .model = fin::model::BlackScholes{.volatility = pluss::make_series({vol})},
                       .controls = {.engine = fin::module::Engine::Analytic}};
  return fin::hedging::delta_hedge(f, path);
}
static double iv(double price, double S, double K, double r, double q, double T, const fin::pricing::ImpliedVolOptions &o = {}) {
  fin::module::Field f{.instrument = fin::instrument::make(fin::pricing::Call, K, T), .market = fin::market::make(S, r, q),
                       .model = fin::model::BlackScholes{.volatility = pluss::make_series({0.2})},
                       .controls = {.engine = fin::module::Engine::Analytic, .risk = fin::module::Risk::PriceOnly}};
  return f.implied_vol(pluss::make_series({price}), o).items<double>()[0];
}

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(12));
  const double S = 100.0, K = 100.0, r = 0.05, q = 0.02, T = 1.0, v = 0.2;

  const double price = bs(prc::Call, S, 110.0, r, q, T, 0.3);
  prc::ImpliedVolOptions brent;
  brent.method = prc::Brent;
  out.writeln("Auto :", iv(price, S, 110.0, r, q, T), ", Brent:", iv(price, S, 110.0, r, q, T, brent));
}
```

### Example 3

A hard case: a deep-out-of-the-money option, where vega is tiny. Every method returns the right volatility to within the tolerance, because a method that fails the tolerance is rescued by bisection.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace prc = fin::pricing;
namespace mod = fin::module;
using pluss::Series;

static double bs(fin::pricing::OptionType type, double S, double K, double r, double q, double T, double vol) {
  fin::module::Field f{.instrument = fin::instrument::make(type, K, T), .market = fin::market::make(S, r, q),
                       .model = fin::model::BlackScholes{.volatility = pluss::make_series({vol})},
                       .controls = {.engine = fin::module::Engine::Analytic, .risk = fin::module::Risk::PriceOnly}};
  return f.price().price.items<double>()[0];
}
static pluss::Series bsv(fin::pricing::OptionType type, const pluss::Series &spots, double K, double r, double q, double T, double vol) {
  fin::module::Field f{.instrument = fin::instrument::make(type, K, T), .market = {.spot = spots, .rate = pluss::make_series({r}), .dividend_yield = pluss::make_series({q})},
                       .model = fin::model::BlackScholes{.volatility = pluss::make_series({vol})},
                       .controls = {.engine = fin::module::Engine::Analytic, .risk = fin::module::Risk::PriceOnly}};
  return f.price().price;
}
static pluss::Series bst(fin::pricing::OptionType type, const pluss::Series &spots, const pluss::Series &tau, double K, double r, double q, double vol) {
  fin::module::Field f{.instrument = {.type = type, .strike = pluss::make_series({K}), .maturity = tau}, .market = {.spot = spots, .rate = pluss::make_series({r}), .dividend_yield = pluss::make_series({q})},
                       .model = fin::model::BlackScholes{.volatility = pluss::make_series({vol})},
                       .controls = {.engine = fin::module::Engine::Analytic, .risk = fin::module::Risk::PriceOnly}};
  return f.price().price;
}
static fin::hedging::DeltaHedgeResult hedge(const pluss::Series &path, fin::pricing::OptionType type, double K, double r, double q, double T, double vol) {
  fin::module::Field f{.instrument = fin::instrument::make(type, K, T), .market = fin::market::make(100.0, r, q),
                       .model = fin::model::BlackScholes{.volatility = pluss::make_series({vol})},
                       .controls = {.engine = fin::module::Engine::Analytic}};
  return fin::hedging::delta_hedge(f, path);
}
static double iv(double price, double S, double K, double r, double q, double T, const fin::pricing::ImpliedVolOptions &o = {}) {
  fin::module::Field f{.instrument = fin::instrument::make(fin::pricing::Call, K, T), .market = fin::market::make(S, r, q),
                       .model = fin::model::BlackScholes{.volatility = pluss::make_series({0.2})},
                       .controls = {.engine = fin::module::Engine::Analytic, .risk = fin::module::Risk::PriceOnly}};
  return f.implied_vol(pluss::make_series({price}), o).items<double>()[0];
}

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(10));
  const double price = bs(prc::Call, 100.0, 180.0, 0.02, 0.0, 0.25, 0.2);
  for (const prc::ImpliedVolMethod method : {prc::Newton, prc::Secant, prc::Bisection}) {
    prc::ImpliedVolOptions options;
    options.method = method;
    out.writeln(static_cast<int>(method), ": price", price, " -> implied vol =", iv(price, 100.0, 180.0, 0.02, 0.0, 0.25, options));
  }
}
```

